  "notes": "Static site: 5 HTML pages (no templating; header/footer duplicated in each), one stylesheet with tokens in :root (styles.css:3-40), one script app.js branching on body[data-page]. Locations were found by text search and id/class search, because there are no data-insp-path attributes. Lines are given for the fixer; they are not identity. Root cause of the inconsistent error borders (F-0064/F-0075/F-0083/F-0015): styles.css:283 styles only input[aria-invalid] (so the #arrive select and the berth radios never turn red). The hover/active rules at styles.css:269-281 (specificity 0,2,1) also outrank the invalid rule (0,1,1), so an errored input under the pointer shows the ink border. That is probably why 'Length' and 'Skipper's name' stayed dark in captures (medium confidence). Confirmation drops the arrival time because app.js:224 forwards only date, nights and berth, and confirmed.html has no time row. MMSI accepts any non-empty value (app.js:181). The date min/max (index.html:45) is ignored because the form is novalidate and app.js:114 checks only that a value is present. The boat form is reset on every pageshow (app.js:165-167) and never reads its query parameters, so any 'change' link back to the boat step would lose the entries. Fixes for F-0033, F-0034, F-0042, F-0049 and F-0050 must handle this. I did not read anything under .eval/ or any builder notes.",
